      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-97682",
      ":question/problem": "In winter, the maximum daily temperature of a certain mountain location (rounded to the nearest degree) varies between $-5^{\u2218}C$ and $10^{\u2218}C$, inclusive. Assuming that for a given winter day, each maximum temperature value between $-5^{\u2218}C$ and $10^{\u2218}C$ has an equal probability of occurring, what is the temperature standard deviation? Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
